{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-08T21:35:26.789Z","data":{"text":"Done. Summary of the work:\n\n**Task 5 complete** — approval now prints notices, gates on opened red notices, and records them in the manifest.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `src/core/spec/digest.ts` — `ApprovalDigest` gains `notices?: ApprovalNoticeRecord` (`{ items, opened }`, declared here with `RecordedNotice` imported as a type); `buildApprovalDigest` never sets it; file kept at exactly 250 lines.\n- `src/core/spec/approve-worktree-shared.ts` — `ApprovalReviewOptions` gains `openedNotices`; `review` becomes `(digest, notices)`; `confirmApproval` builds notices, refuses unopened red notices before review (`open each red notice before approving: <labels>`), and returns the digest with `notices` from `recordNotices` and filtered/sorted `opened` (null when not given). `writeApprovalSeal` passes `digest.notices` through.\n- `src/core/run/manifest.ts` — `ManifestData.notices?` recorded by `buildManifest` next to `approvalFlags`; planning-only manifests omit it (247 lines).\n- `src/cli/approve.ts` — `openedNotices` option (no CLI flag) passed to `approveSpec`; review prints `formatApprovalNotices` one line each before the digest, with and without `--confirm`.\n- `tests/approve-notices.test.ts` — covers every scenario of \"Notices at approval\" and \"Approval notices in the manifest\" through `approveCommand`/`approveSpec` on temporary non-git projects, including the refusal writing neither `.run/approved` nor a manifest.\n\n**Verified:** task verify green (8/8), `pnpm typecheck:cli` clean, biome clean on all five files, all related approval/worktree/stacked/steering/show/manifest/web tests pass (84 + 46 suites), and the proposal-level `pnpm verify` completed with `EXIT:0` (typechecks, build, full test suite, lint)."}}
